{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00012","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00012@rel:R19-11#c29b4aae","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00012","release":"R19-11","content":"AUTOSAR Revision Declaration The AUTOSAR XML descrip- tion shall declare the AUTOSAR revision which was the basis for its creation via the schema location hint URI [TPS_ASR_00013] that is mapped to the AUTOSAR namespace [TPS_ASR_00011] in the xsi:schemaLocation attribute. The attribute xsi:schemaLocation and the declaration of the AUTOSAR schema location hint for the AUTOSAR namespace is mandatory.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_TPS_ARXMLSerializationRules.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:23+00:00","text_key":"b3271cc77ecc","rejoin":{"rule":"text-rejoin@1","e":[[52,2,""]]}}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00012","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R19-11","last_active_release":"R19-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":[],"platform_releases":["R18-10","R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11","text_releases":["R19-11"],"presence_only":[],"unchecked":["R18-10","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"]},"element":{"kind":"requirement","name":"","module":"ASR","cluster":"","page":"","doc_type":"TPS","ai":false,"first":"R19-11","last":"R19-11","changed":[],"distinct":1,"universe":"CP"},"evidence":{"figures":[],"snippets":[],"cited_in":[],"cited_total":0},"id":"TPS_ASR_00012","kind":"element","module":"asr","cluster":null,"platform":"CP"}
{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00013","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00013@rel:R19-11#3beb191b","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00013","release":"R19-11","content":"Pattern for AUTOSAR XML Schema location hint URI The AUTOSAR XML Schema location hint URI in the AUTOSAR XML description shall be the file name of a XML Schema document provided by AUTOSAR. This file name follows the pattern: AUTOSAR_{number}.xsd {number} corresponds to the specific AUTOSAR release the given AUTOSAR XML Schema belongs to. In particular no path shall be part of the AUTOSAR XML Schema location hint URI .","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_TPS_ARXMLSerializationRules.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:23+00:00","text_key":"347f37d267dd"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00013","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R19-11","last_active_release":"R19-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":[],"platform_releases":["R18-10","R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11","text_releases":["R19-11"],"presence_only":[],"unchecked":["R18-10","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"]},"element":{"kind":"requirement","name":"","module":"ASR","cluster":"","page":"","doc_type":"TPS","ai":false,"first":"R19-11","last":"R19-11","changed":[],"distinct":1,"universe":"CP"},"evidence":{"figures":[{"id":"FIG-2ebf5dac312ac081","doc":"AUTOSAR_TPS_ARXMLSerializationRules","p":13,"rel":[],"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"ARCHITECTURAL_CONTEXT","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Shows pattern for XML Schema files.","n":2,"cap":"Figure 2.1: Releases of AUTOSAR standards that are contained in the AUTOSAR XML Schema","sha":"2ebf5dac312ac0817124156426b3c0df9a75393c51ef823e09a227c8238eef3c","nser":2,"src":"figure"},{"id":"FIG-5ffedbac21aea893","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_TPS_MachineConfiguration","p":10,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.8,"rt":"ARCHITECTURAL_CONTEXT","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Metamodel M2 serialization to XML Schema.","n":2,"cap":"Figure 2.1: Visualization of different meta-levels from the serialization perspective","sha":"5ffedbac21aea89346c22df4b6b99f1f325421fc97ff20c7160bcb2155c465dd","nser":2,"src":"figure"}],"snippets":[{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_CLASSICPLATFORMRELEASEOVERVIEW_SECTION_6_2_Release_4_3_1","doc":"ClassicPlatformReleaseOverview","p":48,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.75,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"ARXML Serialization Rules schema location hint pattern.","n":1,"x":"6.2 Release 4.3.1 Revision 1 of Release 4.3.1. has been released on the 8th of December 2017. The following deliverables had major changes. Name Specification history entry Application Interfaces Use…","src":"manifest"}],"cited_in":[],"cited_total":0},"id":"TPS_ASR_00013","kind":"element","module":"asr","cluster":null,"platform":"CP"}
{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00014","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00014@rel:R19-11#38c22360","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00014","release":"R19-11","content":"Sorting elements if their order is semantically meaningless Attributes with upper multiplicity > 1 whose order of elements is semantically mean- ingless (not flagged as {ordered} and not owned by a class with stereotype «atp- Mixed» or «atpMixedString» ) should be serialized using the following heuristics: 1. If the AUTOSAR meta model defines an atp.Splitkey (see [TPS_GST_00050] in [10]) at the aggregation then the contained elements shall be sorted alphabetically in ascending order us- ing a key that is calculated according to the expression mentioned in the atp.Splitkey . E.g. if atp.Splitkey =\" shortName,variationPoint.shortLabel \" then the elements are sorted by a key that is calculated by concatenation of the values of the OCL expressions in the atp.Splitkey : shortName + \",\" + variationPoint.shortLabel . 2. If no atp.Splitkey is defined, then the following ex- pression for calculation of the key is assumed: short- Name,shortLabel,variationPoint.shortLabel . If the shortName , shortLabel or variationPoint.shortLabel is not defined then its value is assumed to be an empty string. If the attribute is of kind reference then the following rule applies 1. The absolute short name path of the referenced target shall be used even if it is a relative reference. See also [TPS_GST_00169] and [TPS_GST_00352] in [10]. The strategy for calculation of the sort key might not be able to calculate unique keys for all sets of elements. This is a known limitation. For those cases the producing tool should define its own custom strategy in order to ensure deterministic serialization of elements for which the order is semantically meaningless.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_TPS_ARXMLSerializationRules.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:23+00:00","text_key":"c0a4d4c634a3","rejoin":{"rule":"text-rejoin@1","e":[[143,2,""],[224,2,""],[490,2,""],[877,2,""],[932,2,""]]}}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00014","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R19-11","last_active_release":"R19-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":[],"platform_releases":["R18-10","R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11","text_releases":["R19-11"],"presence_only":[],"unchecked":["R18-10","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"]},"element":{"kind":"requirement","name":"","module":"ASR","cluster":"","page":"","doc_type":"TPS","ai":false,"first":"R19-11","last":"R19-11","changed":[],"distinct":1,"universe":"CP"},"evidence":{"figures":[],"snippets":[],"cited_in":[],"cited_total":0},"id":"TPS_ASR_00014","kind":"element","module":"asr","cluster":null,"platform":"CP"}
