{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00016","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00016@rel:R19-11#21219b95","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_ASR_00016","release":"R19-11","content":"No empty wrappers Some attributes and references in AUTOSAR models are mapped to a hierarchy of two or more XML elements. The AUTOSAR XML description should not contain incomplete hierarchies. The semantics of those incomplete hierarchies is equivalent to “the value is not set”. This rules applies for attributes, aggregations and references for which the following XML Schema production rules apply [1]: • [TPS_XMLSPR_00008] XML Schema production rule: composite property rep- resentation (1111) • [TPS_XMLSPR_00009] XML Schema production rule: composite property rep- resentation (1101) • [TPS_XMLSPR_00023] XML Schema production rule: composite property rep- resentation (1100) • [TPS_XMLSPR_00022] XML Schema production rule: composite property rep- resentation (1011) • [TPS_XMLSPR_00010] XML Schema production rule: composite property rep- resentation (1001) • [TPS_XMLSPR_00011] XML Schema production rule: composite property rep- resentation (0111) • [TPS_XMLSPR_00012] XML Schema production rule: composite property rep- resentation (0101) • [TPS_XMLSPR_00014] XML Schema production rule: composite property rep- resentation (0011) • [TPS_XMLSPR_00017] XML Schema production rule: reference property repre- sentation with role wrapper element","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_TPS_ARXMLSerializationRules.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:23+00:00","cleaning":{"rule":"spec-text-clean@1","raw_sha256":"21219b956853d030f0ba5967f3beceb13842fdb94e9e3c855215bc629eed6905","removed":["15 of 26  AUTOSAR CONFIDENTIAL  Document ID 779: AUTOSAR_TPS_ARXMLSerializationRules ARXML Serialization Rules AUTOSAR CP R19-11"],"replaced":["U+0093→“","U+0094→”"]},"text_key":"92187b1984f0","rejoin":{"rule":"text-rejoin@1","e":[[477,2,""],[569,2,"